  "interpretation": "Bell landmark submission falls from 26.287 ms to 0.231 ms, and complete 3D submission from 30.296 ms to 4.772 ms. Actual presentation improves 26.42 to 27.72 nominal FPS with 94 to 57 double-length holds; later stages remain 30.00 with every frame held 2 VIs. Do not interpret the submission reduction as eliminating that much total-frame/GPU time: identical geometry still executes on the RSP/RDP. Bell remains below target.",
  "lifetime_and_bounds": [
    "Each source part used by the current map has one aligned, uncached encoded index list, shared by repeated instances. Every triangle restarts the list, keeping exact indices, winding and order. Vertex-load and material-pass ordering are unchanged.",
    "Retained blocks contain geometry commands only. Current camera/matrix, texture uploads, material/filter/depth state remain at their original draw location. Vertex positions, UVs and colours are baked into the existing world-space arena.",
    "begin() drains pending RSP work before freeing blocks/index data or modifying stage geometry; finish() creates new buffers/blocks once per map. No per-frame allocation or fence is added.",
    "Source indices are validated against each batch vertex count. Aligned index DMA is checked against free DMEM using the pinned Tiny3D 70 vertex/36 byte transformed-vertex layout. All 490 current source batches fit (max 32 vertices/87 indices)."
  ],
